parts.body:
§ 2601(a) forbids [[unfair-claims-settlement-practices]] — listed acts committed without just cause and frequently enough to show a general business practice, including:

- knowingly misrepresenting pertinent facts or policy provisions to claimants;
- failing to acknowledge claim communications with reasonable promptness;
- failing to adopt reasonable standards for prompt investigation;
- not attempting in good faith to settle claims where liability is reasonably clear; and
- forcing policyholders to sue by offering substantially less than they ultimately recover.

After receiving a properly executed **proof of loss**, the insurer must advise the claimant of acceptance or denial within **30 working days**. Each instance of noncompliance may be treated as a separate violation for monetary penalties; a violation is not a misdemeanor (§ 2601(c)).
